    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30018" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mūnuscŭlum</span></b> , i,
			n.
		dim.
		munus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a small present</i> (class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">amico munusculum levidense mittere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Fam. 9, 12, 2</span></i>
			: nemini hoc deferre munusculum maluit, quam suo accusatori,
			Cael. ap. <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam. 8, 8, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">8, 12,
			1</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prima munuscula,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					E. 4, 18</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exigit a te nulla munuscula,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv. 6,
					36</span></i>
			.</div>
